 ### Blur Loss
-L2 loss between the simulated blurry image and the input blurry image. The parameter $B(x)$ is the input blurry image at pixel $x$ [S14].
+L2 loss between the simulated blurry image and the input blurry image [S15]. The parameter $B(x)$ is the input blurry image at pixel $x$ [S15].
 
 ### Clipped MSE Loss
-A pixel-wise mean squared loss operating in linear color space (no gamma compression) that handles under-exposed and over-exposed values using a one-sided difference based on clipping thresholds. The parameters are $v_{min}$ (lower clipping threshold) and $v_{max}$ (upper clipping threshold) [S15].
